The one-inch guy is Micro Nick.

Little Nick does not like that name.

He calls him The Witness.

Micro Nick almost never speaks. He just appears in places where Nicolas Cage is making a bad decision about to become cosmically important. On top of a dashboard. Inside a cereal box. Standing on the rim of a wine glass with his tiny arms crossed like he has personally reviewed the timeline and is disappointed.

The problem is, Micro Nick seems to know everything.

Not in a useful way.

He knows the ending of movies nobody has made yet. He knows where lost socks go. He knows exactly what sentence somebody is about to say, but instead of warning them, he just mouths it at the same time and makes everyone uncomfortable.

Once Jessica caught him staring at a microwave.

“What are you doing?”

Micro Nick, barely audible:

“Waiting.”

“For what?”

The microwave hit 0:01.

Micro Nick whispered:

“Now.”

Power went out across three states.

Little Nick immediately dove behind a couch.

“SHIT. HE’S EARLY.”

Apparently, the Cage Limit is recursive.

If regular Nicolas Cage gets too Nicolas Cage, reality produces Little Nick.

If Little Nick gets too Nicolas Cage…

Micro Nick happens.

And nobody knows what occurs if Micro Nick exceeds his own Cage Limit.

Little Nick refuses to discuss it.

Regular Cage asked him once.

“So there’s an even smaller me?”

Little Nick looked genuinely terrified.

“Don’t say that out loud.”

Jessica: “Why?”

Little Nick points toward a salt shaker.

Everybody slowly turns.

Nothing happens.

Long silence.

Jessica exhales.

“This is fucking ridiculous.”

Then a grain of salt moves.

Tiny voice:

“…Jessica.”

She throws the entire shaker across the room.

Regular Cage immediately stands up.

“WE HAVE TO GO.”

“WHERE?!”

“I DON’T KNOW YET.”

Micro Nick, already riding in Cage’s shirt pocket:

“Good. They can’t predict us.”

Little Nick:

“Who’s they?”

Micro Nick looks up.

“…Us.”

And that is currently the deepest level of Cage lore anyone has survived.